-- statement:
--   An auxiliary lemma of the round-six development, published as a separate node because its proof is long or shared.
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.KFWSub`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem NLogN.KFW.RS.touch_sub (σ : Fin HS → Option ℤ) : ∀ (p : NLogN.RS), ∀ i ∈ touch p,
--       i ∈ touch (RS.sub σ p) ∨ (σ i).isSome
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** KFW: literals read from registers (the uniformity meta-theorem for register programs)
--
--   A uniform register program `U` reads its run-time parameters from registers (tops of stacks).
--   `RS.sub σ U` replaces each register `i` with `σ i = some v` by the literal `v`; the result is
--   the (non-uniform) program with baked-in literals, for which a spec is usually already proved.
--
--   **`FSp.of_sub`**: if `FSp (U.sub σ) s t c`, the registers of `σ` hold their values in `s`
--   (`Agree σ s`) and `U` never writes them, then `FSp U s t (400 c)`.  Also `fok_of_sub`.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** Part of the Lean formalization of the round-six κ-improvement (integer-multiplication-kappa campaign, target `IntMul.Kappa.jain_round6_framework`). The statement is copied verbatim from the Lean development; the platform node carries the same declaration name. Definitions it mentions live in the `IntMul_Kappa_R6_Defs*` bundles (on top of the published κ bundles `IntMul_Kappa_K_Defs*`).
